    "title": "Day of the Dead isn't Mexican Halloween",
    "description": "Day of the Dead isn't about being scared. It's about remembering, every November 1st and 2nd.\nFamilies build ofrendas with photos and favourite foods, marigolds are said to guide souls home, and sugar skulls celebrate a person's life. La Catrina started as José Guadalupe Posada's satire of Mexico's upper class, and Diego Rivera made her an icon.",
